WEBVTT

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.060
The sound won't stop.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.370
I shouldn't have looked.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.220
Manabe.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.110
Here.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:19.870
Yasuda.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:20.920
Here.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.640
Yuzuriha.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.630
Yuzuriha?

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.380
Absent again?

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.690
<i>I wonder what happened to Yuzu.</i>

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.060
<i>He didn't come to practice
this morning, either.</i>

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.380
<i>This has never happened before.</i>

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.390
No new messages.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.390
<i>He hasn't tried to message or call me.</i>

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:48.440
Jeez...

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.030
Just when I thought she was learning 
to mind her own business,

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.320
she goes into my room without asking again.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.720
Why do you have partially 
written music in your room?

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.490
You promised me you'd never 
get involved with music again!

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.080
Stop this!

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:04.000
It has no meaning!

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:16.280
I couldn't make it to morning practice.

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:20.720
No! I have to think about something fun!

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:21.970
Yuzu.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:23.220
Yuzu.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.230
We're friends, right?

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:31.110
Friends, huh?

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.990
It's gonna hurt if I fall 
for her any more than this.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:12.420
♭07 Our Lines of Sight Finally Overlapped

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:22.220
Nino: Yuzu, are you sick?

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.350
<i>Sorry, Alice.</i>

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.650
<i>I don't want to see you today.</i>

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.430
I'll have to change my strings soon.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:36.480
Yeah?

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.620
Bass strings are so expensive.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.490
I wonder why.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.090
Not here.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.200
What?!

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.500
But it was like—

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.130
Nino?

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:47.880
Not here.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:52.620
Hey, what are you up to, Nino?

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:55.690
I haven't been able to 
contact Yuzu all morning.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:58.380
Huh? Doesn't that happen all the time?

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:01.590
Not here.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:14.980
Crap, it's getting dark.

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:18.160
What should I do?

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:20.710
I don't think I can go home.

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:22.660
But Haruyoshi lives too far away,

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:24.690
and Kuro is probably busy 
at his part-time job.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:25.550
Eyelashes?

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.490
Yeah, it really is you.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:29.960
Sakaki?

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:32.450
Oh, that's right. You live around here.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.160
What are you doing here?

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.450
Uh, er... no real reason.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:39.210
Running away?

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.080
You're in the apex of youth, huh?

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.700
Apex-choo!

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.090
Are you making fun of me?!

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:49.560
Wanna come to my place?

00:04:57.010 --> 00:05:02.480
<i>The number you have dialed is either 
out of the service area or turned—</i>

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.070
No new messages.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.180
Thanks for having me.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.380
Sit wherever.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.060
Coffee okay with you?

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.250
I'm not a fan of coffee.

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.380
Oh, right. Milk's your thing.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.670
I-I can drink coffee!

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.670
Here, it's coffee with a milk ratio of 1:9.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.350
That's basically just milk!

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.730
Would you rather play tough 
with strong coffee?

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:29.930
Stop it with the puns!

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:34.730
It's good.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:37.250
So? Why'd you run away from home?

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.240
It's not a big deal.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.700
Oh. Did they find your porn?

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:42.930
That's not it!

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:46.390
Music isn't allowed in my home, but my 
mom found out I was writing music.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:48.240
Not allowed? Why?

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:54.190
My mother's abnormally afraid of 
letting me get involved in music.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:57.000
I once had to repeat a year 
because of conflict over that.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.610
That's why there's nothing 
related to music in our house.

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:03.750
I'm used to it now, though.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.680
You're older than me?

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.010
That's the part that gets you?

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.830
She checks my computer and phone every day.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.010
Of course, I delete the history, but...

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.090
Can't you set a password?

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:17.760
That's not allowed, either.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:20.120
You could make it, like, 
"moojuice" or something.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.150
I said it's not allowed!

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:26.650
The only places I can play 
music are school and...

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.900
Come with me, Eyelashes.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:38.620
You want to play, don't you?

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.830
Amazing!

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.330
You compose here?

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:44.150
Yeah.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:47.050
Sometimes I do it elsewhere, but mostly here.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.840
It's a Jazzmaster! I want one of those!

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.760
What kind of songs do you write?

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.650
Well, I guess songs for women.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:55.010
Seriously? Me, too! Why?

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:56.350
Doggy...

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:55.950
<i>Doggy...</i>

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:00.850
Originally, I was making them 
for a childhood friend.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:05.360
But recently, someone took her 
from me, and it made me angry.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:09.610
She was supposed to belong only to me.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:15.110
Is she... the girl you like?

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.440
That's not it.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.810
You don't have anyone you like?

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:20.760
I dunno.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:23.990
But you have someone you like, don't you?

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:25.270
How do you know?

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:26.330
Because you drink milk.

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:27.130
That's how?!

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:31.010
With that personality of yours, 
I bet you're not very assertive.

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:32.310
How did you know?!

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.010
Stop acting like such a pushover.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:39.900
Try something like, "I'm a man, you know. 
You never know what I'll do to you."

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:41.520
In what situation would I do that?!

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.740
Think about that yourself.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:44.230
You're not doing a good job of this!

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:47.980
Assertive, huh? You're pretty strong.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.950
I bet you never get jealous.

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:52.480
Are you stupid? Of course I do.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:55.490
But I don't bottle it up. 
I let it out with music.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:01.920
You're the same, right?

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:22.630
What song is that?

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:25.030
Just one of the many I wrote today.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.940
Yeah? Sounds like it wouldn't sell, 
in a good way.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.210
It sounds like it won't sell?!

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:29.780
Huh?

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:31.240
It doesn't smell like money?

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.970
N-Nope, not at all.

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:38.780
It sounds like you just impulsively threw 
all your feelings into it or something.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:40.890
Is that right?

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:45.170
I can play it?

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:46.790
Sure.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:21.220
Oh, yes.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:25.460
Hello?

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:26.710
Right.

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:28.620
The second song.

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:29.290
Yes.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:30.960
This is bad.

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:34.990
I really want to see you right now,

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:37.420
Alice.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:44.480
12 new messages.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.980
Alice
Alice
Alice
Alice
Alice
Alice
Alice

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:47.780
This many?

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:48.840
What happened?

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.730
Incoming Call 
Alice

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:53.410
Hello?

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:54.190
<i>Yuzu?</i>

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:55.990
Y-Yeah... What's the matter?

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:58.740
I got through.

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:00.740
I got through.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:05.360
Right. About that...

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:08.010
Yes.

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:09.480
That's right.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:11.470
Thanks, Sakaki!

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:12.600
I'll come by again!

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:14.920
Talking
Tsukika-san

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.470
Oh, hello? Sorry about that.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:21.180
I just had a friend over.

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:34.150
Yuzu!

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:37.480
Alice!

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.280
What's the matter, Alice? You're a mess.

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:48.000
I was worried since you didn't 
come to morning practice...

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.230
And I couldn't reach you all day.

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:54.840
I... I asked Miou and the rest, 
and they didn't know anything.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:57.820
They laughed at me, saying there 
was nothing to worry about.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:00.040
But I was just so, so worried, 
for some reason.

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.460
I couldn't help it.

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:03.850
Are you okay?

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:08.300
I was worried something had
happened, like six years ago,

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:09.980
and you'd disappeared again.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.140
I was so scared.

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:14.400
So scared.

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:20.530
Let me see your face.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:24.500
I'm so relieved that nothing's wrong.

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:32.010
Your mask slipped off.

00:11:32.010 --> 00:11:33.880
Oh, you're right.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.780
And your hair's a mess.

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:37.050
It is.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:41.300
Have you been looking for me all this time?

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:50.060
Don't look at me.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:51.560
Yuzu?

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:54.710
Don't look at me like that.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:56.690
Huh?

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:00.260
Uh, Yuzu, I can't see.

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:04.450
Huh? Yuzu? Yuzu? I can't see a thing.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:05.960
Did you shrink?

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:09.510
In NO Hurry's a real eyesore.

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:12.460
Yes, of course.

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:15.050
I'll show no mercy. I'll crush them.

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:20.460
Have you guys seen this?

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:23.170
Silent Black Kitty.

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:24.880
It's Kiryuu's new band.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:26.920
They're a masked band,

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:30.460
and their debut album comes out the 
same day as In NO Hurry's first album.

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:32.890
They even have "black cat" right in their name!

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.300
<i>This is the band from that audition.</i>

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:36.770
What's more...

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:49.190
<i>This crazy feeling full of lies</i>

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:54.280
<i>A plastic memory, falling apart</i>

00:12:56.330 --> 00:13:00.050
<i>Virtual discord that won't stop echoing</i>

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.460
<i>I'm falling silent!</i>

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:08.630
It's alternative. Same as us.

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:12.450
Isn't Kiryuu Momo the guy
who wrote idol songs?

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:14.270
He can write songs like this, too?

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.370
The instrumental parts are amazing.

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:17.770
Especially the drums.

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:19.540
Is this the time for praise?

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:20.770
<i>The bassist...</i>

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:22.780
<i>It's Momo.</i>

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:25.290
<i>He's actually a member of the band?</i>

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:30.530
Wait a minute. The vocalist...

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.540
Yeah. That's me.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.330
What?!

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:38.900
I told Yuzu that I got through the audition.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:40.290
But I didn't hear about this!

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:41.990
Congrats, Miou! I guess.

00:13:41.990 --> 00:13:43.550
You guess?!

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.720
That's great! I guess.

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:47.800
Miou's gotten really good.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:46.850
You guess?!

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:47.800
I guess.

00:13:51.590 --> 00:13:52.310
Hello?

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.690
<i>Hello, this is Yana.</i>

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.750
<i>It's lunch right now, right? 
So you're all there?</i>

00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:57.100
Huh? Yeah.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:59.350
<i>Put me on speaker and turn down the volume.</i>

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:06.570
Talking
Yana

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:03.520
<i>The top summer music festival,</i>

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:06.570
<i>Rock Horizon, has confirmed
an appearance by In NO Hurry.</i>

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:10.290
<i>I'm sure you've already seen 
the rip-off band online.</i>

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:13.070
<i>That annoying black cat will be there, too.</i>

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:15.190
<i>So you're looking at a direct showdown.</i>

00:14:15.190 --> 00:14:17.960
<i>But more importantly, 
it'll be your first live concert.</i>

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:22.840
Talking
Yana

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:20.380
<i>You know what this means, right?</i>

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.840
We do. Obviously...

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.360
We're gonna crush it!

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.090
<i>Direct showdown?</i>

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.340
<i>In other words, at this festival,</i>

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:31.440
<i>I can see Momo!</i>

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:36.100
I didn't mean to hide the 
fact that I was accepted.

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:39.210
But they said I couldn't say anything 
until the information was released.

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:41.460
More like, why are we the rip-off band?

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:44.030
Damn that Yana! He even knew I got accepted!

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:45.370
I'm so pissed off!

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:46.940
Con—

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:50.690
Congratulations on being accepted.

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:52.490
That sounded pretty forced.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.890
I know you're actually frustrated.

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:57.480
That's not true! I went in knowing I'd fail.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:58.800
Did you really?

00:14:58.800 --> 00:14:59.480
Did...

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:02.580
Did you talk to Momo?

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:03.580
Yep.

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:05.150
Was he cool?

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:08.250
What's that supposed to mean? 
Well, I guess he's the popular type.

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:09.260
Miou...

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:13.300
Don't fall for Momo, okay?

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:18.550
You're starting to seem more human!

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:19.880
What are you talking about?

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:22.360
I've been a human since the day I was born.

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:27.400
Anyway, about Rock Horizon...

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:29.180
It might be perfect for you.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:34.410
Did you know that Rock 
Horizon has three stages?

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:38.560
And from the biggest stage, you can 
see all the way to the horizon.

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:40.270
Didn't you once say that

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:42.420
you wanted to reach the entire globe?

00:15:43.030 --> 00:15:47.170
I want to change my voice into something 
that'll reach everyone around the globe.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:51.440
Back then, I was thinking, 
"What's with this girl? What an idiot."

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:56.730
But if you sing on that stage, won't it feel 
like your song will reach the entire globe?

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:12.690
<i>Miou's good at playing guitar.</i>

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:15.200
<i>And her voice is totally different 
than it was at orientation.</i>

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:17.200
<i>This was the voice</i>

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:19.120
<i>that made Momo</i>

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:21.000
<i>look her way that day.</i>

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:25.520
<i>I want to get better.</i>

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:28.470
<i>I want to get better.</i>

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.270
<i>I want to get better.</i>

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:37.220
<i>When I shout, that alone makes me invincible</i>

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:35.270
<i>I want to get better by summer.</i>

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:37.970
<i>And then, for sure,</i>

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:39.760
<i>I'll make you look.</i>

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:44.100
What happened to your fingers?

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:46.040
I played too much over the weekend.

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:48.270
Your voice sounds kind of hoarse, too!

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.640
No practicing today.

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:50.940
Why? I want to practice.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.820
Don't forget that you're a pro now!

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:55.820
Sorry.

00:16:56.720 --> 00:17:00.200
I was just so preoccupied 
thinking I could see Momo again.

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:01.810
Momo?

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:04.070
Momo was in that band.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.310
So I realized I could 
see him at Rock Horizon.

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:12.780
So I thought, this time for sure, 
I have to make him look my way.

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:17.300
I was in too much of a rush, 
and could only think about myself.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.600
I'm so embarrassed.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:23.020
I can't believe I was in such a rush 
that I couldn't see anything around me.

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:24.180
I'm sorry.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:26.450
I understand. All too well.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:28.630
When your fingers and voice get better,

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:31.060
I can give you vocal and 
guitar lessons after school.

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:35.490
J-Just so you know, it's because 
I have no other choice!

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:39.250
You'll go too far if I leave you alone, 
so you've left me no choice, got that?

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:40.880
Yuzu.

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:41.790
What?

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:43.790
Thanks.

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:48.160
I won't say you're short anymore!

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:49.510
What's that got to do with it?!

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:57.040
You're late, Eyelashes.

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:59.480
It's my first time coming 
to the S-class building.

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:01.930
Turns out it's right next to our building.

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:03.810
Do you come to the roof often?

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:06.090
Yeah, since I can be alone up here.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.580
Anyway, what did you want to talk about?

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:11.480
I just came to thank you for the other day.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:14.940
Liar. I bet you want to talk 
about that girl you like.

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.390
How did you know?!

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:19.700
Out with it. I'm busier than a busy bee.

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:26.060
Sakaki, h-have you ever 
asked a girl out before?

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:27.510
Is that what you're gonna do?

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:30.330
Well, more like, lately...

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:33.210
I feel like I might just 
accidentally tell her...

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:34.380
that I like her.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:37.600
So you're confessing that the time 
to confess is getting near?

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:39.280
I hate you!

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:40.510
Why not just tell her?

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:43.350
You just keep bottling everything up.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:45.310
Before you do something weird,

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:47.020
isn't it better just to let it all out?

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:51.020
You think so?

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:54.270
We finally got through everything.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:56.540
But I still make lots of mistakes.

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:59.470
You've got a good feel for everything, 
so I think you're almost there.

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:00.600
Really?

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:03.230
Well, it's mostly all thanks to me, though.

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:04.880
I won't say you're short anymore.

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:06.420
Just drop it already!

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:08.020
You're amazing, Yuzu.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:13.250
You always get through difficult
things like this so easily.

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:14.860
I admire that.

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:16.510
I respect you.

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:18.750
Th-That was no big deal, really.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:21.980
<i>We will be arriving shortly 
at Kamakura. Kamakura.</i>

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:24.260
L-Look, Alice, we're here. 
We have to get off—

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:31.440
<i>The doors on line one are closing.</i>

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.410
<i>Be careful of closing doors.</i>

00:19:59.110 --> 00:20:02.520
<i>Next is the last station, Zushi.</i>

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:06.670
Crap! I fell asleep! I missed our stop!

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:10.930
Whoa! I fell asleep, too! What a shock!

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:10.930
Now we've done it!

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:22.130
Alice.

00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:27.140
Can we do tomorrow's morning 
practice on the roof?

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:29.820
I don't mind, but why?

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:39.640
There's something I want 
to talk to you about.

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:47.400
<i>I wonder what he wants to talk about.</i>

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:50.140
<i>He had a really serious look on his face.</i>

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:54.130
<i>Amazing. I haven't messed up once!</i>

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:54.820
<i>Go!</i>

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:56.730
<i>Go!</i>

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:03.170
I did it! I played it!

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:03.860
<i>I did it!</i>

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:06.240
<i>I'm so happy.</i>

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:12.040
<i>I did it!</i>

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:13.610
<i>I did it!</i>

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:23.140
<i>I'm so happy, Yuzu!</i>

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:25.840
Fly!

00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:33.590
Alice.

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:35.560
I'll tell you.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:38.320
Before you see Momo...

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:40.270
I'll tell you!

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:45.240
<i>I'm always there when I wake up</i>

00:21:46.390 --> 00:21:51.010
<i>You say that's fine if everyone's there</i>

00:21:46.470 --> 00:21:47.820
<i>Yuzu, I can play it.</i>

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:49.390
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:21:50.690 --> 00:21:51.500
<i>Hurry.</i>

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:54.990
<i>So come here with me</i>

00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:54.320
<i>Hurry.</i>

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:57.350
<i>I want to see you.</i>

00:21:56.580 --> 00:22:01.340
<i>When I shout, that alone makes me invincible</i>

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:00.890
<i>Momo!</i>

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:05.340
<i>So please don't open this cage</i>

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:19.150
<i>It's been six years</i>

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:21.900
<i>since I first heard your voice and cries.</i>

00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:24.810
Alice!

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:25.650
Momo.

00:22:32.860 --> 00:22:34.040
<i>Today,</i>

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:36.410
<i>our lines of sight finally</i>

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:41.240
<i>overlapped.</i>

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:52.120
♭08 
I Will Be Your Friend, I Swear I Will
